# R12: Arthur Lockwood, the spectral infant in the nursery (H13). Speaker arthur_lockwood; quest arthurs_bear; memento memento_blue_bear / memento_bear
# (taken from the crib by ch_quasits, not here). Arthur has no words: wails and babble; the Narrator carries the scene.
# FINAL-WORDED: every Narrator and character line below is voiced; no line changes once the voice lane starts (new lines are fine).
# The bear is the memento whether or not he is calmed. Calming (Persuasion DC 15, or Performance DC 15 as a lullaby) earns Heroic Inspiration, arthur_rested
# and the cutscene ch_arthur_sleeps; a hero who heard Patrini's lament sings with the tune it left. The patient way (sit with him an hour) also settles him,
# without the Inspiration, so a bad roll never closes the quest.
# NOTE (contract gaps): (1) dialogue checks cannot carry Advantage, so the lament's Advantage on the lullaby is written as DC 10 for the book's DC 15 (the same
# chance for a typical hero); (2) the contract has no "heard the lament" flag, so flag.memento_key stands for it (the key only pops out after Patrini plays the
# lament at the harpsichord, in either of its ways).
# Wiring assumptions: Arthur is placed `when: not flag.arthur_rested`; the prop h13_crib starts ch_quasits; this conversation starts arthurs_bear at `wailing`
# (the quest's giver is Arthur) and moves it to bear_taken once the bear is the party's.
# Drafted by Gemini (gemini_r12_arthur/brief.md, reply_raw.json), edited; see that folder's README.md.

~ start
if flag.arthur_rested
-> done
endif
if not (quest.arthurs_bear == wailing or quest.arthurs_bear == bear_taken)
quest arthurs_bear wailing
endif
if flag.memento_bear
quest arthurs_bear bear_taken
endif
if item:memento_blue_bear
-> calm
endif
-> wail

~ wail
Narrator: That cry gets right into your back teeth and sets the floorboards hummin' under your boots.
Narrator: A little blue ghost hovers over the mahogany crib, pale tears driftin' up toward the ceiling.
arthur_lockwood [sad]: Waaah... uh-waaah!
Narrator: His tiny hands close on empty air, reaching out for a piece of comfort that ain't there.
arthur_lockwood [sad]: Ba... ba! Waaah!
interject class:cleric: No child ought to be left crying in the cold like this.
interject class:fighter: Keep your voices down and your hands easy, all of you.
* Try to hush him with kind words. -> hush_empty
* Leave him be for now. -> END

~ hush_empty
Narrator: Your words go in one ear and right out the wail, because a baby wants what a baby wants.
-> END

~ calm
Narrator: The blue bear in your hands is worn threadbare, with one button eye hangin' by a single stitch.
Narrator: That long cry climbs a note, catches on a breath, and stops dead while he stares at the toy.
arthur_lockwood [sad]: Hic... ba?
* [Persuasion DC 15] Speak low and steady, and tell him the bear has come home. -> calm_ok | calm_miss
* [if flag.memento_key] [Performance DC 10] Sing him the harpsichord's lament as a lullaby. -> lullaby_ok | lullaby_miss
* [if not flag.memento_key] [Performance DC 15] Sing him a lullaby. -> lullaby_ok | lullaby_miss
* Sit down with him and the bear, and wait it out. -> patient
* We will come back to him. -> END

~ calm_ok
Narrator: You pitch your voice low and steady as a banked stove on a frosty night.
Narrator: Little by little, the wail unravels into long, shaky breaths that barely stir the dust.
arthur_lockwood [smile]: Guh... ba...
inspire party: soothed a crying child with kind words
-> asleep

~ calm_miss
Narrator: The cry swells up anew and the old house shivers round you, windowpanes rattling in their frames.
arthur_lockwood [afraid]: Waaah! Waaah!
-> calm

~ lullaby_ok
Narrator: Your song goes out thin and plain, and even the cold lamp seems to lean in a spell to listen.
Narrator: The blue glow in the little fellow settles down from a hard boil to a gentle simmer.
arthur_lockwood [smile]: Oooh... mm...
if flag.memento_key
Narrator: Then the harpsichord tune from the music room slips into your voice, and his heavy eyes follow it down.
endif
inspire party: sang a crying child to sleep
-> asleep

~ lullaby_miss
Narrator: Your voice cracks on the third bar and the wail comes back louder, shakin' the shelf of stuffed toys.
arthur_lockwood [afraid]: Buh... waaah!
-> calm

~ patient
time +60
Narrator: You sit yourself down on the cold boards with the bear across your lap and don't say nothing clever.
Narrator: A whole hour goes by in small shushin' sounds and the creak of the roof timbers overhead.
Narrator: Even a ghost gets tired, it seems, and the cry runs down one breath at a time like a clock nobody winds.
arthur_lockwood [weary]: Hhh... ba.
-> asleep

# The picture is a hero's arms, no face, cradling the glowing infant; then empty arms and blue motes. The bear stays with the party.
~ asleep
cutscene ch_arthur_sleeps
Narrator: He settles into your arms as light as lamp-glow, one tiny fist wrapped tight round that loose button eye.
Narrator: For the first time in a long age, the whole crooked house goes quiet from eaves to cellar.
cutscene ch_arthur_sleeps_2
Narrator: He thins out until you are holdin' nothing but warmth, and then that warmth lifts away in small blue sparks.
arthur_lockwood [smile]: Ba...
Narrator: Now only the old blue bear rests in your hands, a good deal heavier than it looks.
cutscene end
set arthur_rested
quest arthurs_bear asleep
approve tobin_hayward +2 rook_coldwake +1 lucan_houndstooth +1: You settled a restless child to sleep
-> END

~ done
Narrator: The mahogany crib is just a crib again, the nursery sits still as a held breath, and a faint smell of warm milk and lamp oil hangs in the air.
-> END
